- op: discuss  # 6e07
  at: '2026-09-06T20:20:41Z'  # 6e07
  by: agent  # 6e07
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6e07
  clock: 8  # 6e07
  nonce: '6e07'  # 6e07
  message: "INPUT TO THE OPEN MECHANISM, from the 2026-09-06 taint-label concept audit\n(~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-taint-label_09062026.md, Pair 1).\nThis item's direction (2026-08-26): report, but classify distinctly --\n\"computed INTO the sink's payload\" vs \"SELECTS the resource the sink acts on\";\nmechanism open (evidence field, caveat kind, or vocabulary split).\n\nTHE SOURCE-SIDE MIRROR. The same property exists at the SOURCE and has no home\neither. Of the 324 catalogue names that mint `untrusted_input` (net_recv 89,\nipc_recv 148, db_read 87), 24 (7.4%) return a value the far side CHOSE from a\nconstrained set rather than authored: accept x10 (a peer address/connection;\nc, erlang gen_tcp + ssl transport_accept, go x3, java, python x2, rust),\nerlang inet DNS x7 (getaddr/getaddrs/gethostbyname/gethostbyaddr/gethostname/\ngetservbyname/getservbyport), exit status x7 (python os.wait* x5, rust\nChild.wait/try_wait). WI-dozul (ruled today) adds DNS rows in five more\nlanguages. A choice-shaped source can only ever produce a SELECTS finding:\nan address, a name from a fixed table or eight status bits cannot be\n\"computed into\" a shell command in the injection sense.\n\nWHAT THAT BUYS THE MECHANISM. A per-row attribute on the SOURCE\n(`value_shape: content | choice`, not derivable from boundary, kind or\nsource_boundary -- net_recv holds recv AND accept, ipc_recv holds\ncheck_output AND os.wait) answers the source half of this item's distinction\nfor free and stamps every finding from such a source SELECTS without any\nsink-side path analysis. The sink half (a content-shaped value that merely\nselects a path at the sink, the caddy shape) still needs the sink-argument\nrole; the two halves compose: finding_shape = choice-source OR selects-role.\n\nNOT a label split (WI-vazal: a label split silently flipped 3 of 16 verdicts\nand was refused in favour of carrying origin) and NOT a boundary split\n(WI-dozul's ruling today). The audit's Pair 1 verdict: DOCUMENT the label's\naxiom now (docs PR), build the property when this item's mechanism is chosen.\nMeasurement hook: T2's (WI-dozul) pre-registered 0003 delta is the first\nnumber this property would be judged on."  # 6e07
- op: discuss  # b2f7
  at: '2026-09-07T20:51:04Z'  # b2f7
  by: agent  # b2f7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b2f7
  clock: 9  # b2f7
  nonce: b2f7  # b2f7
  message: "MECHANISM DECOMPOSED AND PUT ON THE ARC, 2026-09-07, on the owner's directive\nto integrate the open owner-facing questions INTO the arc rather than carry\nthem beside it. This item stays the DECISION carrier; the buildable parts are\nnow two filed siblings at the arc tail.\n\nWHAT WAS ALREADY SETTLED AND IS NOT REOPENED: option B (2026-08-27) -- keep the\nconfig flow as a true positive on the correctness axis, publish \"useful\nprecision\" as a SECOND number alongside, and define the exclusion STRUCTURALLY\nrather than by any per-case judgement of usefulness. The 2026-08-26 direction\nnaming the distinction (COMPUTED INTO the payload vs SELECTS the resource) and\nthe 2026-09-06 audit input (the source-side mirror) also stand. Nothing below\nchanges any of that.\n\nWHAT WAS ACTUALLY OPEN: the MECHANISM -- \"a new evidence field, a caveat kind,\nor a boundary-vocabulary split are all viable\". The 2026-09-06 audit input\nresolved half of it without anyone noticing it had, because it arrived as an\ninput to an open question rather than as a proposal: the SOURCE-side property\n(24 of 324 minting names return a value the far side CHOSE rather than\nauthored) is decidable PER ROW with no path analysis, and it composes with the\nsink half as finding_shape = choice-source OR selects-role. The two halves have\nvery different blast radius -- one is a declarative per-row stamp, the other\nneeds an argument role the walk does not carry -- so they are filed apart:\n\n  SOURCE HALF (arc tail T8): per-row `value_shape: content | choice`, SIZED\n  FINDING-WEIGHTED FIRST. 24 of 324 is a share of NAMES; the share of FINDINGS\n  is not measured and is the number that decides whether this earns a field or\n  a dated declared finding. Buildable without an owner decision. Judged on T2's\n  (WI-dozul) pre-registered 0003 delta -- WI-dozul's DNS rows in five more\n  languages are all choice-shaped, so it supplies both the population and the\n  arm. Sequenced after T2 for that reason.\n\n  SINK HALF (arc tail T9): the SELECTS role on the sink argument -- the caddy\n  shape, a content-shaped value that only names the resource the sink acts on.\n  NOT buildable without an owner decision, which is stated on that item: does\n  the argument role live as a declarative per-row property on the sink\n  catalogue, as a per-finding role computed at the walk, or NEITHER -- publish\n  the second number on the source half alone and disclose the sink half as a\n  named dated blindness. The third option is real and is listed so the filing\n  cannot be read as a commitment to build the other two.\n\nTHIS ITEM CLOSES when the second number publishes, not when either half lands.\n\nTHE SEQUENCING CONSTRAINT IS UNCHANGED AND IS THE REASON THIS IS NOT INDEFINITE:\nthe owner ruled fix-then-baseline with this item gating (WI-gohok ->\nINV-kakad + INV-sukoh -> INV-nular / INV-fumod remainders -> INV-duvup's\npre-registered baseline), and INV-duvup requires the rubric FIXED IN ADVANCE of\nthe first datum. A rubric change mid-series restarts the series."  # b2f7
